## Build 8h-b closes the three measured serving-coverage blockers between the 2.3% census and the ~85-90% the physics supports (heavy-saddle qd tail is 8h-c, out of scope). Three levers, each sized by a quoted measurement: (1) per-cell measured ceilings in the ppGO map via truncation-on-refusal — recovers the 30 invalidated cells (the largest single coverage bucket, killed today because one refusing angle at w~66 invalidates a whole cell); (2) a fold-gated ghost-pair subtraction giving a v3 far-field label E = F − Σ_real H_a e^{iwτ_a} − G, where G is the decaying complex-conjugate quartic-root pair, gated on w·Im τ_c and cusp windows, plus component-grid node reprovisioning on the smoother remainder; (3) caustic-fixed interior coordinates (ρ=|y|/r_caustic(γ,θ)), per-lobe saddle interior frames, and a crown (γ≈0.87-0.99) representation switch from the ill-conditioned far-field-style interior label to the SACR-C τ_c-demodulated envelope label. In-build acceptance is FAST synthetic-scale (mechanisms + Test-Developer domain tests + tube byte-identity); the map v2 sweep, serving census, calibration re-pilot, and full campaign are POST-BUILD driver steps in the brief's order. ASSUMPTIONS documented: scratchpad/complex_saddle_probe.py is absent from the worktree, so P1/P2 probe numbers are taken as given (per brief). The ghost gate ships conservatively at w_min·Im τ_c≥2 and the crown milestone at eps 3.4→≤1e-1 (order of magnitude); the re-pilot measures the tighter optima. WP5 (node reprovision) is kept as a small standalone mechanism WP rather than folded into WP4 (Simplifier suggested folding) to keep the riskiest WP4 focused and to make the campaign/mechanism boundary explicit; WP8's design is Professor-pinned (SACR-C envelope label), not an open design question.

### WP1: ppGO map: truncation-on-refusal + per-cell w_ceiling schema + loader hard-refusal
  What: Recover cells that today are invalidated when any angle refuses at any w. Replace the whole-cell-invalidate behavior in _measure_cell with truncation-on-refusal: per angle, find the maximal accepted w-prefix and certify on it; store a per-cell w_ceiling = min-over-angles alongside w_cert. Add the w_ceiling grid to the artifact with a schema/provenance bump; the loader hard-refuses maps lacking it.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/ppgo_map.py (_measure_cell ~L608, CertifiedPpgoMap schema/from_arrays/load ~L202-427, build_map ~L706, save_map ~L796, provenance/_content_hash ~L178); scripts/train_ppgo_map.py (producer — coarse/production edges unchanged); .claude/spec/DATA_CONTRACTS.yaml (certified_ppgo_map schema entry ~L226).
  How: The saddle-image-branch refusal is MONOTONE in w (refuses for all w above a ceiling: 'Saddle wave branch refused: w=66.05 exceeds ceiling'), so the accepted set is a PREFIX [w_min, w_ceiling]. In _measure_cell, per angle: bisect on the w_nodes PREFIX-ENDPOINT INDEX (integer k) — evaluate the engine on w_nodes[:k], which either succeeds or raises a refusal (LensDomainError/CancellationError/SchwingerCertificationError); bisect k to the maximal accepted prefix. This is O(log n_w) engine evaluations per angle, NOT a full re-sweep per step. Then compute the existing sup-over-w floor (_sup_over_w_floor) on the accepted prefix only; the cell's w_cert stays the min-clearing floor over the accepted range, and w_ceiling = min over angles of each angle's max accepted w. A cell certifies on its measured range even when its top-w refuses; BEYOND the ceiling stays UNKNOWN — never extrapolate. Distinguish a per-angle refusal that truncates (new behavior) from a genuine engine error unrelated to the w-ceiling: only the named refusal vocabulary triggers truncation; anything else still invalidates (keep the STATUS_INVALID path). Add w_ceiling to: the (2,n_gamma,n_rho) grid family, from_arrays, save_map's np.savez, load's array read + KeyError-guarded required-key check, and _content_hash / _hash_scalars (so a ceiling-less or tampered artifact fails the hash and use_certified_ppgo_map returns False — the 8g-b tag philosophy). Bump provenance schema_version and add a 'w_ceiling_rule' description string. Add a w_ceiling(parity,gamma,rho) accessor that mirrors w_cert/w_trust EXACTLY (returns the stored ceiling for certified cells, UNKNOWN out-of-grid) — reuse the existing UNKNOWN sentinel, do NOT invent a new sentinel semantics. Update the DATA_CONTRACTS.yaml certified_ppgo_map description to name the w_ceiling grid and the truncation-on-refusal semantics. Use `python scripts/pipeline_graph.py consumers_of certified_ppgo_map` to confirm the consumer list before finalizing the schema (WP2 consumes it).
  Who: Coder
  Verification: _measure_cell truncates on the monotone saddle-branch refusal and certifies the accepted w-prefix instead of invalidating the whole cell; every certified cell carries a finite w_ceiling and the artifact/loader/hash include the w_ceiling grid; a map artifact missing the w_ceiling grid or with a mismatched hash causes use_certified_ppgo_map to return False (global stays None); the w_ceiling accessor mirrors the w_cert UNKNOWN-sentinel pattern with no new sentinel; DATA_CONTRACTS.yaml names the new grid.
  Max turns: 75

