### WP3: Ghost-kernel machinery: decaying complex-saddle pair + analytic-continued kernel
  What: Add a dedicated complex-saddle ('ghost') path in geometry: extract the decaying complex-conjugate quartic-root pair that the image finder currently discards, and compute its carrier-free ghost kernel by analytic continuation of the delay and amplitude formulas to the complex root position. This is the physics primitive the v3 label (WP4) subtracts.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/geometry.py (_generic_candidates ~L646 complex-root filter, delay ~L267, hessian/magnification ~L296, image_kernel ~L913, morse_index ~L317, _saddle_metric + _c1_polynomial/_c2_polynomial ~L823-910, critical_point ~L945).
  How: Professor-pinned construction (this is load-bearing; do NOT reroute through the real-only kernels). The ghost pair is literally the two roots _generic_candidates rejects at its `abs(raw_root.imag) > tolerance` cut — the u_c→x_c map (x_c = source_radius·[(a22−u_c), −a12]/det) is complex-analytic, so continuation is exact and free. Add a helper to return the complex root pair from the same companion-matrix solve and SELECT the decaying member by Im τ_c > 0 (so e^{iwτ_c}=e^{iw Reτ_c}·e^{−w Imτ_c} decays). Implement a SEPARATE `_ghost_kernel(x_c, matrix)` (do NOT call delay/image_kernel/morse_index — they use real-only ops np.linalg.norm, sqrt(abs(μ)), eigvalsh): (a) delay via the complex Fermat potential — the lens term is ½·clog(x_c·x_c) with the BILINEAR x_c·x_c=x1^2+x2^2 (a complex number) and a COMPLEX log; pin the branch by continuity from the real fold image (where x·x>0, principal branch) and track arg(x_c·x_c) continuously off the caustic — a 2π slip is a full carrier-phase error; (b) amplitude = 1/sqrt(det H_c) where H_c is the bilinear-continued Hessian (matrix − I/(x·x) + 2 x⊗x/(x·x)^2, all bilinear), on the branch fixed by requiring H_c → H_saddle continuously as the pair approaches the real fold — track arg(det H_c) unwrapped from the real saddle's sqrt|μ|·e^{−iπ/2} and take sqrt on the unwrapped phase; the Morse phase is NOT a separate integer factor here, it is ABSORBED into this square-root branch (calling morse_index on a complex Hessian double-counts); (c) multiply the C1/C2 series continued verbatim (pure polynomials in the complex _saddle_metric). Expose Im τ_c so WP4 can gate on w·Im τ_c. Add explicit shape/branch-continuity guards and specific named exceptions for the degenerate near-fold limit; document the reference (Fermat potential + fold/saddle-point continuation) and units (dimensionless w, τ).
  Who: Coder
  Verification: geometry exposes a decaying-ghost extractor (complex-conjugate pair from the quartic, Im τ_c>0 member) and a dedicated _ghost_kernel computing τ_c via complex-log delay, amplitude 1/sqrt(det H_c) on a branch continued from the real fold, and C1/C2 continued; the ghost path never calls image_kernel/delay/morse_index; the ghost magnitude AND phase reproduce the P1 fold-annulus beat (R/E in 0.038-0.14 for w≥3-8) at an anchor config.
  Max turns: 95

