### WP6: Caustic-fixed interior coordinate (astroid): directional radius admission + cusp-ray tiling
  What: Replace the single inscribed-disk interior admission with the directional caustic radius ρ=|y|/r_caustic(γ,θ_y), making admission exact across a γ band (no band-edge waste). Tube-shell exclusion uses the nearest-caustic distance; tile boundaries align to the four astroid cusp rays so no tile straddles a kink.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/surrogate_training.py (_caustic_inradius ~L1032, _farfield_interior_tiles ~L1069, interior admission in _train_band_charts ~L1938); cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/geometry.py (critical_point ~L945, caustic sampling — add an r_caustic(γ,θ) directional-radius helper).
  How: Professor-pinned. Add a geometry helper r_caustic(γ,θ) = source-plane caustic radius along the ray at angle θ (from critical_point sampling). Interior admission becomes exact enclosure: a tile is interior iff its farthest point has ρ=|y|/r_caustic(γ,θ_y) < 1 across the tile — replacing the isotropic admit_radius=inradius−eta_max disk that throws away the anisotropic interior between inradius and the directional radius. TWO caveats: (i) r_caustic(θ) has KINKS at the four astroid cusp rays (shear-axis and diagonal directions), so ρ is non-smooth across them — ALIGN tile boundaries to the four cusp rays so no tile straddles a kink (a straddling tile carries a non-analyticity subdivision cannot rescue); keep the existing cusp-window exclusion as the safety net. (ii) Admission uses the DIRECTIONAL radius, but the tube-shell margin (the eta_max exclusion) must use the NEAREST-caustic-point distance, not the radial one — near a cusp the nearest caustic is off the radial ray, so a radially-interior tile could still be within eta_max of a cusp. Concretely: admit with directional ρ<1; exclude the tube shell with nearest_caustic distance. Preserve the existing origin-enclosure / winding topology gate (astroid encloses origin; saddle handled in WP7). Document units (dimensionless y, ρ) and the r_caustic(θ) sampling density.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: Interior admission uses ρ=|y|/r_caustic(γ,θ_y) so a point just inside the directional caustic radius admits and just outside refuses for every γ in a band (no band-edge waste vs the old inscribed disk); tube-shell exclusion uses nearest-caustic distance; no admitted tile straddles one of the four cusp rays; the astroid origin-enclosure gate is preserved.
