### WP8: Crown interior label: SACR-C τ_c-demodulated envelope + finer crown γ-bands
  What: Near γ→1 (crown, γ≈0.87-0.99) the far-field-style interior label is ill-conditioned (subtracts individually-divergent near-merged image kernels → eps=3.4 catastrophe). Switch interior crown tiles to the SACR-C τ_c-demodulated envelope label (channel switch ON) so the near-critical images are switched into a bounded envelope rather than subtracted; add finer interior γ-bands near γ=1. Tag the interior-envelope tiles so the serve side reconstructs correctly.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/channels.py (partition.envelope SACR-C transition label ~L1094, _channel_switch ~L357, reconstruct_from_envelope ~L639); cogwheel/lensing/surrogate_training.py (interior chart build + gamma-band splitting stable_gamma_bands ~L716, gamma_band_halfwidth ~L250); cogwheel/lensing/surrogate.py (envelope-definition tag frozenset ~L137, _validate + npz meta ~L1332).
  How: Professor-pinned — the design is FIXED, not open. Diagnosis: the far-field-style interior label E=F−Σ_real H_a e^{iwτ_a} subtracts four individually-blowing-up kernels (sqrt|μ_a|→∞ at the sharpening cusps) whose coherent sum is finite — a difference of large near-cancelling terms, so eps=3.4 is fitting cancellation noise, and densification would fit garbage more finely (forbidden). Fix: interior crown tiles use the EXISTING SACR-C interior label (partition.envelope: channel switch ON, τ_c-demodulated) so near-merged images (small w·|τ_a−τ_c|) are switched into the bounded envelope instead of subtracted — this is the bounded-phase, well-conditioned object SACR-C was built for. This is a LABEL choice; the interior COORDINATE stays WP6's caustic-fixed ρ (do NOT adopt tube (u=√η,θ) coordinates). Add a distinct interior-envelope tag to the frozenset, set it on interior crown tiles, and have reconstruct_from_envelope dispatch on it (add the switched channels back at τ_c). Add finer interior γ-bands near γ=1 (tighten the crown band split) — but note finer γ-bands are hygiene, NOT the fix (eps=3.4 is a fixed-γ conditioning error, not a γ-interpolation error). Falsifiable in-build bar: a synthetic mid-γ=0.40 interior tile that FAILS at eps=6.0e-2 under the far-field-style label PASSES the 1e-3 gate under the SACR-C label; crown milestone (conservative, in-build): interior eps drops from ~3.4 to ≤1e-1 (order of magnitude). Whether the crown reaches 1e-3 or plateaus at ~1e-1 (a genuine cusp/Pearcey higher-catastrophe needing the deferred cusp-uniform program) is measured by the POST-BUILD re-pilot — do NOT attempt the Pearcey local model in this build.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP6
  Verification: Interior crown tiles use the SACR-C τ_c-demodulated envelope label (switch ON) instead of the far-field-style label, in WP6's caustic-fixed coordinate, with a distinct interior-envelope tag the serve side dispatches on; a synthetic mid-γ=0.40 interior tile that fails at 6.0e-2 under the far-field-style label passes the 1e-3 gate under the SACR-C label; the crown interior eps no longer shows the 3.4 catastrophe (drops ≤1e-1); finer crown γ-bands are added; no Pearcey local model is introduced.
  Max turns: 75

### Professor Inputs
  - The ghost pair is exactly the complex-conjugate quartic roots that geometry._generic_candidates discards at its imag-tolerance filter; the u_c→x_c map is complex-analytic so continuation is exact and free. Select the decaying member by Im τ_c>0.
  - Do NOT reuse image_kernel/delay/morse_index for the ghost (real-only ops). A dedicated _ghost_kernel: delay via ½·clog(x_c·x_c) with BILINEAR x·x and a COMPLEX log branch pinned by continuity from the real fold; amplitude 1/sqrt(det H_c) on an unwrapped-arg branch seeded at the real saddle; the −iπ/2 Morse phase is ABSORBED into that sqrt branch (calling morse_index double-counts); C1/C2 continue verbatim.
  - Ghost gate currency is w·Im τ_c radians (mirrors SACR-C RHO_END=4), NOT absolute Im τ_c. Ship conservatively: apply G at w_min·Im τ_c≥2, keep v2 at <1, plus the cusp-window mask (geometry degrades before Im τ_c hits 0). On-axis Im τ_c=0 ⇒ refuse. The exact optimum is a post-build re-pilot sweep over {0.5,1,1.5,2,3}.
  - Reachable-red configs: HELPFUL γ∈{0.2,0.4}, off-cusp ρ∈[1.2,1.8], w∈[3,40] ⇒ eps_v3≤eps_v2/3 (3-6× measured); HARMFUL γ=0.4 on-cusp ρ≈1.05-1.15, w∈[3,20] ⇒ gate refuses AND forced-G grows the residual.
  - Node reprovisioning: reuse LOO _heldout_eps (F-normalized 1e-3 bar) on the v3 remainder; the probe DECIDES the node budget (don't hardcode ~2×). The ghost smooths ONLY the w-axis (a carrier e^{iwτ_c}); H_c(y),τ_c(y) still vary, so HOLD y1/y2 tiling density — coarsening risks straddling a fold turnover.
  - Interior coordinate ρ=|y|/r_caustic(γ,θ_y) gives exact enclosure (endorsed), but r_caustic(θ) has cusp KINKS: align tile boundaries to the four astroid cusp rays; use the DIRECTIONAL radius for admission but the NEAREST-caustic distance for the tube-shell margin (near a cusp the nearest caustic is off the radial ray).
  - Per-lobe saddle: each deltoid lobe gets its own interior family in a lobe-local frame with origin at the SOURCE-PLANE deltoid centroid (a regular point, not a critical point); 3 cusp rays per lobe; assign by nearest centroid and exclude the inter-lobe equidistance corridor (a flip line analogous to the astroid diagonal).
  - Crown eps=3.4 is a LABEL-CONDITIONING failure (subtracting individually-divergent near-merged kernels), not a γ-interpolation error, so densification and finer γ-bands alone provably cannot reach 1e-3. Fix = the SACR-C τ_c-demodulated interior envelope (switch ON) which is bounded by construction. Falsifiable bar: mid-γ=0.40 tile failing at 6.0e-2 under the far-field label PASSES 1e-3 under the SACR-C label; crown milestone eps 3.4→≤1e-1 in-build, with the residual to 1e-3 owned by a deferred post-build cusp/Pearcey uniform program.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - ppGO truncation-on-refusal certifies a top-w-refusing cell. Setup: a synthetic _measure_cell scenario (monkeypatched/engine-stubbed) where the saddle-image branch refuses monotonically above some w* at one or more angles. Operation: run the cell measurement. Expected: the cell is CERTIFIED on [w_min, w*] with a finite stored w_ceiling ≈ min-over-angles(w*), NOT STATUS_INVALID; w_cert is the sup-over-w floor on the accepted prefix only. Diagnostic: plot per-angle accepted-prefix endpoint vs angle — a whole-cell invalidation shows w_ceiling absent/NaN. Mutation check: with truncation disabled the cell must go INVALID (reachable-red).
  - Cell-ceiling band-split guard (reachable-red both ways). Setup: install a coarse map whose cell has ceiling C strictly below the parity wall W. Operation: dispatch two draws, one with w_hi in (C, W) and one with w_hi < C. Expected: the (C,W) draw does NOT band-split (falls through to the whole-band refuse path, bare ppGO never serves beyond-ceiling nodes); the w_hi<C draw band-splits normally. Contrast: with the ceiling ignored (parity-wall-only, HEAD behavior) the (C,W) draw would wrongly split — that must be the red state.
  - Loader hard-refuses ceiling-less / tampered maps. Setup: a map artifact with the w_ceiling grid removed, and a second with a mutated w_ceiling value (hash mismatch). Operation: call use_certified_ppgo_map on each. Expected: both return False and leave the global map None (every query returns UNKNOWN); a well-formed map with the grid loads and its w_ceiling accessor returns finite ceilings for certified cells and UNKNOWN out-of-grid.
  - Strata trim respects the ceiling. Setup: a stratum whose top w exceeds the cell ceiling, and one whose top w is below it. Operation: run the strata trim. Expected: the first is KEPT intact (its beyond-ceiling tail is UNKNOWN and must stay charted/refused, not handed to ppGO); the second is dropped/capped as before. Diagnostic: the recorded trim action per stratum ('drop'/'cap'/'keep').
  - Ghost reproduces the P1 beat and smooths the remainder (helpful config). Setup: fold-annulus configs γ∈{0.2,0.4}, source off-cusp at θ_y≈45°, ρ=|y|/reach∈[1.2,1.8], w-band [3,40], β=0,κ=0. Operation: build the v3 label E=F−Σ_real H_a e^{iwτ_a}−G and compare its spline remainder to the v2 label at EQUAL node count. Expected: G matches the E_ff beat in magnitude AND phase with R/E in 0.038–0.14; the v3 remainder eps ≤ v2 eps / 3 (RN16 anchor: v3 1.3e-3–2.5e-3 vs v2 7e-3–1.4e-2). Diagnostic: overlay |E_v2| and |E_v3| vs w — v3 should be visibly beat-free.
  - Cusp-window gating is harmful-inside / helpful-outside (reachable-red both ways). Setup HARMFUL: γ=0.4, source ON the cusp axis (on-axis), ρ≈1.05–1.15, w∈[3,20] so Im τ_c≈0. Setup HELPFUL: the fold-annulus config above. Operation: evaluate the training-time gate and, separately, force-apply G. Expected HARMFUL: the gate REFUSES G (w_min·Im τ_c<1 and inside the cusp window) and force-applying G GROWS the residual (eps_v3 > eps_v2, e.g. ≥1.5×). Expected HELPFUL: the gate APPLIES G and eps shrinks ≥3×. This proves the gate fires in the correct direction on both sides.
  - Serve mirror reconstructs F for a v3 tile. Setup: a trained v3 tile at a helpful config. Operation: serve the envelope and reconstruct F via reconstruct_from_envelope with G added back analytically (same decaying-member selection and t_min carrier). Expected: |F_reconstructed − F_exact| / max|F| within the 1e-3 F-normalized bar across the band; the ghost carrier decay e^{−w Im τ_c} matches. Diagnostic: reconstruction error vs w.
  - Mixed v2/v3 artifact routes by tag. Setup: one artifact containing both a v2 tile and a v3 tile, plus a tile with an absent/unknown envelope tag. Operation: load and serve each. Expected: each tile reconstructs correctly via its own label path (v2 two-kernel, v3 ghost add-back); the absent/unknown tag is hard-refused at load; the mixed artifact is legal (no coexistence validation error).
  - Ghost-kernel branch correctness against an INDEPENDENT oracle (non-circular). Setup: an anchor fold config. Operation: compare the code's ghost τ_c (complex-log delay) and amplitude 1/sqrt(det H_c) to an independent re-derivation — e.g. a direct complex quartic-root solve plus a finite-difference complex Hessian determinant, computed WITHOUT reusing the module-under-test's ghost functions (add/confirm an AST guard forbidding those names). Expected: agreement in BOTH magnitude and phase (confirming the branch continued from the real fold and the −iπ/2 Morse phase is correctly absorbed, not double-counted). This targets the complex-log branch-cut and sqrt-branch pitfalls.
  - Node reprovisioning runs on the v3 remainder and is consumed. Setup: a synthetic v3 remainder tile at a helpful config. Operation: run the adaptive per-axis reprovisioning routine. Expected: it reduces the w-node count until LOO _heldout_eps just clears the 1e-3 F-normalized bar, records the per-axis node recommendation in the chart provenance, and the tile builder consumes it; the y1/y2 tiling density is NOT coarsened. Diagnostic: eps-vs-w-node-count curve crossing the bar; assert the recommended w-node count is strictly below the v2 default while y1/y2 counts are unchanged.
  - Caustic-fixed interior admission is exact across a γ band. Setup: an astroid γ band; source points placed just inside and just outside the directional caustic radius r_caustic(γ,θ_y) at several θ_y and several γ in the band. Operation: run interior admission with ρ=|y|/r_caustic. Expected: every just-inside point admits and every just-outside point refuses, with no band-edge waste (contrast: the old inscribed-disk admit_radius wrongly rejects the anisotropic interior between inradius and directional radius). Diagnostic: admission map over (|y|,θ_y) vs the true caustic curve.
  - Cusp-ray tile alignment. Setup: candidate interior tiles including one deliberately placed across an astroid cusp ray (r_caustic kink). Operation: generate the interior tiling. Expected: no admitted tile straddles a cusp ray (tile boundaries align to the four cusp rays); the deliberately-straddling tile is split or excluded; tube-shell exclusion uses nearest-caustic distance (a radially-interior tile within eta_max of a cusp is excluded).
  - Per-lobe saddle admission (reachable-red between lobes). Setup: γ>1 with two deltoid lobes; source points inside lobe A, inside lobe B, and in the inter-lobe corridor on the shear axis. Operation: run per-lobe interior admission. Expected: points inside each lobe admit to that lobe's family (lobe-local frame at the source-plane deltoid centroid, per-lobe winding), the inter-lobe corridor point REFUSES, and real_mask by Morse signs is correct (four→two images across the caustic). Diagnostic: per-lobe winding number and Morse-sign real_mask at each point.
  - Crown SACR-C interior label passes where the far-field-style label fails (falsifiable design bar). Setup: a synthetic mid-γ=0.40 interior tile in the caustic-fixed coordinate, wave band w∈[0.05,20]. Operation: gate the tile under (a) the far-field-style interior label and (b) the SACR-C τ_c-demodulated envelope label (switch ON). Expected: (a) fails at eps≈6.0e-2 (matches the measured baseline); (b) PASSES the 1e-3 gate. Additionally, on a crown γ≈0.9 interior tile the SACR-C label drops eps from the ~3.4 catastrophe to ≤1e-1 (order-of-magnitude milestone). Diagnostic: eps under each label; the contrast is the reachable-red proof that the win is representational, not resolution.

